      "message": "Rename the product to Ambolt\n\nThe working name is retired. The crates are ambolt-core, ambolt-git,\nambolt-server and ambolt-client, the binary is ambolt, and every\nsetting, cookie, token prefix, header and piece of text says so.\nNothing anyone holds stops working: tokens are matched by hash, so\nthe ones already minted still open the door; a setting under its old\nCAIRN_ name is still read for one release, with a word in the log;\nand the receipts that lived under refs/notes/cairn are carried to\nrefs/notes/ambolt the first time the forge starts, the old ref left\nin place so a rollback has nothing to undo. Sessions are the one\nthing that ends: the cookie changed its name, so everyone signs in\nonce more.\n\nThe addresses the forge answers at are not in this change; they move\nwhen the new host does. Version 0.1.0-alpha.2, because an operator's\nunit file names the binary.\n\nChange-Id: Irename0120\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
